# The 8-way terrain scroller: off the carrier, flying flat out (2.5 px a frame)
# north, then south-west, then east: the terrain moves the other way, smoothly,
# across tile columns, tile rows and the ring's wrap.
# Classic steering: left/right turn (a step every 4 frames), up thrusts.
# Each leg is measured over land and coast (Coral Reach's middle island): the
# open-sea tiles are sparse and repeat every 16 px, too little to track.
wait-serial "AGK t0" 3000   # (the floppy loads run after the splash: seconds)
wait 10
press fire 2
wait-serial "theatre loaded=0"
# (the theatre card first: a fresh press of fire skips it)
wait 3
press fire 1
wait 24
hold up
wait 150
release
press left 13
hold up
wait 90
# north along the island's east coast: the strip left of the gunship
expect-scroll 0 0 110 215 140 0 5/2
release
press left 21
hold up
wait 60
# south-west across the island: the rows under the gunship's shadow
expect-scroll 0 165 319 215 140 7/4 -7/4
screenshot southwest
release
press left 21
hold up
wait 90
# east along its south coast
expect-scroll 0 0 319 70 140 -5/2 0
release
expect-no-serial "AGK ERR"
